the number of people hospitalized with  flu like symptoms is now the highest  it's been in almost a decade new numbers  released by the CDC show an estimated 51  out of every 100,000 Americans have been  admitted for the flu this season our  doctor Tara Narula he's here with the  impact of this unrelenting epidemic Tara  good morning good morning John while flu  activity is easing up in the West the  rest of the country remains at high risk  the elderly are being hit the hardest  and the death toll continues to rise at  least 53 children have already died 16  of those died last week alone everybody  is devastated as you've never expected  to happen to you  an Indiana family is in shock after the  sudden death of seven year old Savannah  Jesse the local coroner's office  confirms the first grader tested  positive for influenza strep throat and  scarlet fever before she died  Courtney Hargett is Savannah's aunt he  was so smart smartest little girl you  would ever meet she's always so funny  and fun-loving she was really a free  spirit her father found her unresponsive  one day after taking her to the hospital  after they left the hospital he took her  home put her in bed and then found her  these cases are becoming more frequent  in Virginia 7 year old Kevin Baines died  just one day after testing positive for  the flu and six year old Emily muth from  North Carolina died three days after an  influenza diagnosis both children did  not get the flu shot it's very important  if you notice that a person is getting  better from their flu and then suddenly  gets worse for them to seek medical  attention the signs of getting worse  would be difficulty breathing that  suddenly comes on or spike in the fever  a dominant and dangerous strain of the  flu virus h3n2 is partly to blame for  the nationwide outbreak a recent  Canadian study found that the flu  vaccine is only 17% effective at  protecting against h3n2 it wouldn't  surprise me if we find the same thing  here in the u.s. even with low  effectiveness against h3n2 viruses we  think it's very important to be  vaccinated there have been more than  126,000 confirmed flu cases  but officials say we still may not have  reached the peak of this outbreak and  there is a financial strain as well this  flu season could reportedly cost us  businesses more than 15 billion dollars  in productivity loss Gail why no silver  linings in this story at all thank you  very much Tara
 

